 ## Background
-The 3DGS algorithm is not hardware-friendly and faces four main design challenges, including substantial memory usage [S1]. To overcome these limitations, a dedicated hardware accelerator for real-time rendering of 3DGS models on portable AR/VR devices was introduced, targeting full-HD resolution at 120 FPS per eye [S1]. The compression pipeline is a key component of this accelerator, modifying the lightweight model, LightGaussian, to higher compression ratios [S1].
+The 3DGS algorithm is not hardware-friendly and faces substantial memory usage challenges due to millions of Gaussians in unbounded scenes [S1]. To enable real-time rendering on portable AR/VR devices at full-HD resolution and 120 FPS per eye, a dedicated hardware accelerator was introduced [S1]. This compression pipeline is a core component, modifying the LightGaussian lightweight model to achieve higher compression ratios for hardware deployment [S1].
 
